.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-EXTEND" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-extend - Move a durable tunnel's expiry to now plus a duration


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel extend <tunnel> --duration <time> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Move a durable tunnel's expiry to now plus --duration, for example 24h. Use it when
pb tunnel status says the tunnel expired; it serves again once the change applies.

.PP
A change returns once the request is accepted, and the tunnel may still be connecting. Pass
--wait to wait (at most --timeout, default 2m, 1s to 10m) until it finishes, or check pb tunnel
status.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--duration\fP=0s
	new lifetime from now, for example 24h

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for extend

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=2m0s
	maximum time to wait for operation completion

.PP
\fB--wait\fP[=false]
	wait for the operation to reach a terminal state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb tunnel extend web --duration 720h
  pb tunnel extend tunnel_abc123 --duration 24h --wait
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel(1)\fP
